@Chris

GAUNT is a word. It means "haggard." (I had MERLE at first, but that's irrelevant.)

GAUNT and "haggard" both mean sort of emaciated or sickly-looking. GAUNT especially might mean looking yellowish, depleted, exhausted, weak- or thin-looking, etc. Coffee probably won't help.

