@RL

I perfectly understand that some people’s dislike of rebuses, but I can never understand the use of the word lazy to describe it. Please elaborate. These constructors had to come up with the idea of the revealer, find common phrases with JAM in it, cross them with food that might have JAM in it, and build a grid around it—this seems like a lot of work.

As a constructor I will admit that I still find constructing rebuses easier than a decent themeless—but that’s true of any themed puzzle, I think. And I will admit that rebus puzzles sometimes allow you to enter more quality, longer fill in the grid since you need fewer squares—but that seems like a positive. Neither of these would lead me to call them “lazy”. So please enlighten me more.

